  libraries) are distributed under the Intel Simplified Software
  License: https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/articles/license/onemkl-license-faq.html
  On Windows, the Intel Fortran run-time libraries (libifcoremd,
  libmmd, svml_dispmd) are redistributed under the Intel oneAPI
  redistribution terms.

- The GNU Fortran and GCC run-time libraries (libgfortran, libgcc),
  statically linked on Linux and macOS, are licensed under the GPL
  version 3 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception
  (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gcc-exception-3.1.html), which permits
  their use in programs under other licenses.

- The GCC quad-precision math library libquadmath, statically linked
  on Linux and macOS, is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
  License, version 2.1 (https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html).

- On macOS, the LLVM OpenMP run-time library libomp is licensed under
